ulture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JYCV03BW1S0RTE5/pjd_1K454XKBV1S0V399/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 15 Aug 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KJY9XXRH1S0WQWQ?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JYCV03BW1S0RTE5/pjd_1KZCCWZ191S03KP1/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JYCV03BW1S0RTE5/pjd_1KP6EDJN71S0MK8A/ghg_statement.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JYCV03BW1S0RTE5/pjd_1KZCCVYA21S0W9YQ/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JYCV03BW1S0RTE5/pjd_1KA1F2HER1S0E398/ghg_statement.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JYCV03BW1S0RTE5/pjd_1KZCCTAVX1S0T1ME/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nEW\\n1,000Y+\\nDarjeeling Revival: Alt x MOL\\nAlt Carbon\\nISSUED\\n2,986.72\\nBUFFER POOL\\n59.735\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Oct 2024 to 01 Oct 2029\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThe project is anchored in regions where high rainfall, humidity, and warm summers accelerate silicate mineral dissolution and other key geochemical processes. It sequesters atmospheric CO₂, while enhancing soil health, improving productivity, strengthening the local economy, preserving biodiversity, and advancing sustainable land management practices.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nE3D1\\nApproval date\\n22 Sep 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nDarjeeling Revival: Alt x MOL\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n15 Aug 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 2,765.37 tCO₂e removed from Darjeeling Revival: Alt x MOL on 05 Feb 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n2,765.372 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n3,072.577 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n307.205 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nDRP_Basalt\\tMineral & rock\\t14 Nov 2025\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n14 Apr 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n14 Apr 2026\\tGHG Statement\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n14 Nov 2025\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n14 Nov 2025\\tGHG Statement\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n22 Sep 2025\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 7\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n2,986.72\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n59.735\\nCrediting period\\n01 Oct 2024 to 01 Oct 2029\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n14 Apr 2026\\t2,765.37\\t55.308\\t2,710.062\\n14 Nov 2025\\t221.35\\t4.427\\t216.923\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Alt Carbon's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 59.735 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 191.335 certificates.\\n\\nAlt Carbon has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"